{title: The Bonnie Banks o’ Loch Lomond}
{artist: Tradiční}

{comment: Verse 1}
By [G]yon bonnie [Em]banks and by [C]yon bonnie [D]braes
Where the [G]sun shines [Em]bright on Loch [C]Lo[D]mond
[C] [Em] [Am] [C]*
Where me and my true love were ever wont to gae
[D7]* [G] [Em] [Am]* [D]* [G] [G]
On the bonnie, bonnie banks of Loch Lo - mond

{comment: Chorus}
Oh! [G]Ye'll tak' the [Em]high road, and [C]I'll tak' the [D]low road
And [G]I'll be in [Em]Scotland a[C]fore [D]ye
[C] [Em] [Am] [C]*
But me and my true love will never meet again
[D7]* [G] [Em] [Am]* [D]* [G] [G]
On the bonnie, bonnie banks o' Loch Lo - mond

{comment: Verse 2}
'Twas [G]there that we [Em]parted, in [C]yon shady [D]glen
On the [G]steep, steep [Em]side o' Ben [C]Lo[D]mond
[C] [Em] [Am] [C]*
Where in purple hue, the hieland hills we view
[D7]* [G] [Em] [Am]* [D]* [G] [G]
And the moon coming out in the gloam - ing

{comment: Chorus}
Oh! [G]Ye'll tak' the [Em]high road, and [C]I'll tak' the [D]low road
And [G]I'll be in [Em]Scotland a[C]fore [D]ye
[C] [Em] [Am] [C]*
But me and my true love will never meet again
[D7]* [G] [Em] [Am]* [D]* [G] [G]
On the bonnie, bonnie banks o' Loch Lo - mond

{comment: Verse 3}
The [G]wee birdies [Em]sing, and the [C]wildflowers [D]spring
And in [G]sunshine the [Em]waters are [C]slee[D]ping
[C] [Em] [Am] [C]*
But the broken heart it kens nae second spring again

[D7]* [G] [Em] [Am]* [D]* [G] [G]
Tho' the waeful may cease frae their grie - ving

{comment: Chorus}
Oh! [G]Ye'll tak' the [Em]high road, and [C]I'll tak' the [D]low road
And [G]I'll be in [Em]Scotland a[C]fore [D]ye
[C] [Em] [Am] [C]*
But me and my true love will never meet again
[D7]* [G] [Em] [Am]* [D]* [G]
On the bonnie, bonnie banks o' Loch Lo - mond
